'' T47, RUN: a method that overrides is virtual only if it also says 'virtual' -- fbc's
'' rule, where tiko used C++'s. A plain re-declaration under a non-virtual override HIDES
'' it; 'virtual' over a closed slot opens a new one; a level that declares nothing leaves
'' the slot open; a sibling overload hides the inherited ones; and a destructor overrides
'' only a DIRECT base's virtual destructor. Output identical to fbc-modern's.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/override-not-virtual.bas -o tests/codegen/overridenotvirtual.exe
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-FILE: tests/codegen/overridenotvirtual.exe
'' RUN: tests/codegen/overridenotvirtual.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: override, then plain:   B
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: virtual override, plain: C
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: virtual over closed:     B C3
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: skip a level:            C4
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: hidden overload:         B.n A.s
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: plain middle:  ~B~A
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: no middle:   ~A
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: virtual mid:  ~G ~F~A
